  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Double Wall – round the cone and a one-timer",
  "description": "Three lines in one half: A in the corner by the goal line, B diagonally in front of the goal on the same side and C on the other side. A cone on the same side, a little before the centre line. A passes to B and runs towards the cone. B plays it back, A rounds the cone with the ball and passes to C. Then A sprints towards goal, gets a first-time pass from C and shoots first time.\n\nRotation: A to B, B to C and C to A. Run it mirrored and switch between forehand and backhand passes.\n\nEasier variants: A gets the ball back from B, rounds the cone and shoots alone (no C), or A starts with the ball, rounds the cone, passes to C and gets a first-time return to shoot (no B). The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Round the cone tightly with the ball close to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Switch between forehand and backhand passes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Sprint towards goal straight after the pass to C – the one-timer should hit the target."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
